title: 'pallet-scheduler: postpone overweight tasks instead of silently dropping them'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A scheduled task is now treated as permanently overweight (emitting `PermanentlyOverweight` and
    no longer retried) only when its weight exceeds `9/10` of `Config::MaximumWeight`, meaning it
    could never fit into a block. Any other task that does not fit into the current block is
    postponed to a later block instead of being silently dropped, replacing the previous heuristic
    that gave up on a task merely because it was the first one serviced in the block.

crates:
- name: pallet-scheduler
  bump: patch
